c data flows, and port usage mismatches.","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0538#AN1483","platforms":["Windows"],"tuning":[{"field":"AllowedTools","description":"Whitelist legitimate tunneling tools (e.g., used by admins)."},{"field":"DataAsymmetryThreshold","description":"Ratio of sent vs received bytes that indicates tunneling activity."},{"field":"TimeWindow","description":"Correlate process creation with network connection within N seconds."}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0082","component":"Network Connection Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=3, 22","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN1483","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0538#AN1483","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=1","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN1483","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0538#AN1483","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"}]},{"id":"AN1484","name":"Analytic 1484","guidance":"sshd, socat, or custom binaries initiating port forwarding or encapsulating traffic (e.g., RDP, SMB) through SSH or HTTP. Defender sees abnormal connect/bind syscalls, encrypted traffic on ports typically used for non-encrypted services, and outlier traffic volume patterns.","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0538#AN1484","platforms":["Linux"],"tuning":[{"field":"ForwardingFlags","description":"Specific sshd config flags indicating port forwarding."},{"field":"ProtocolBaseline","description":"Define expected application protocols by port to catch tunneling mismatches."}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0082","component":"Network Connection Creation","name":"auditd:SYSCALL","channel":"socket/connect calls showing SSH processes forwarding arbitrary ports","platforms":["Linux"],"analytic_id":"AN1484","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0538#AN1484","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"component_id":"DC0038","component":"Application Log Content","name":"linux:syslog","channel":"sshd sessions with unusual port forwarding parameters","platforms":["Linux"],"analytic_id":"AN1484","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0538#AN1484","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0038/"},{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"linux:osquery","channel":"socat, ssh, or nc processes opening unexpected ports","platforms":["Linux"],"analytic_id":"AN1484","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0538#AN1484","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"}]},{"id":"AN1485","name":"Analytic 1485","guidance":"launchd or user-invoked processes (ssh, socat) encapsulating traffic via SSH tunnels, VPN-style tooling, or DNS-over-HTTPS clients. Defender sees outbound TLS traffic with embedded DNS or RDP payloads.","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0538#AN1485","platforms":["macOS"],"tuning":[{"field":"ExpectedDoHResolvers","description":"Known legitimate DoH resolvers used in environment."},{"field":"PayloadEntropyThreshold","description":"Flag excessive randomness in payloads on standard ports."}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"macos:unifiedlog","channel":"process execution of ssh with -L/-R forwarding flags","platforms":["macOS"],"analytic_id":"AN1485","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0538#AN1485","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0085","component":"Network Traffic Content","name":"macos:unifiedlog","channel":"encrypted outbound traffic carrying unexpected application data","platforms":["macOS"],"analytic_id":"AN1485","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0538#AN1485","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0085/"}]},{"id":"AN1486","name":"Analytic 1486","guidance":"VMware daemons or user processes encapsulating traffic (e.g., guest VMs tunneling via hostd). Defender sees network services inside ESXi creating flows inconsistent with management plane traffic, such as SSH forwarding or DNS-over-HTTPS from management interfaces.","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0538#AN1486","platforms":["ESXi"],"tuning":[{"field":"ESXiServiceProfiles","description":"Baseline allowed services and expected ports for ESXi management."}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0078","component":"Network Traffic Flow","name":"esxi:vpxd","channel":"ESXi processes relaying traffic via SSH or unexpected ports","platforms":["ESXi"],"analytic_id":"AN1486","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0538#AN1486","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0078/"},{"component_id":"DC0085","component":"Network Traffic Content","name":"esxcli:network","channel":"listening sockets bound with non-standard encapsulated protocols","platforms":["ESXi"],"analytic_id":"AN1486","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0538#AN1486","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0085/"}]}]}],"telemetry_references":[{"id":"DC0038","name":"Application Log Content","tag":"Application Log Content","page":"telemetry/DC0038/","kind":"attack_component"},{"id":"DC0082","name":"Network Connection Creation","tag":"Network Connection Creation","page":"telemetry/DC0082/","kind":"attack_component"},{"id":"DC0085","name":"Network Traffic Content","tag":"Network Traffic Content","page":"telemetry/DC0085/","kind":"attack_component"},{"id":"DC0078","n